WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(electronic music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.890
- [Jason] Anything you
can do on a snowboard,

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.742
you can do on a mountainboard.

00:00:03.742 --> 00:00:05.380
(loud rocks)

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:08.670
I love the feeling of being in nature

00:00:08.670 --> 00:00:11.038
and charging down the mountain.

00:00:11.038 --> 00:00:12.980
(intense drum music)

00:00:12.980 --> 00:00:15.070
I wanted to keep that
feeling all year round,

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:18.140
so we built what's called a mountainboard.

00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:42.000
(electronic music)

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:44.550
My name is Jason Lee,
and I'm Creative Director

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.120
for MBS Mountainboards.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.363
I've done mountainboarding for 27 years.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:52.390
A mountainboard is a

00:00:52.390 --> 00:00:55.320
combination of a skateboard, a snowboard,

00:00:55.320 --> 00:00:56.416
even a mountain bike,

00:00:56.416 --> 00:00:58.020
all rolled into one

00:00:58.020 --> 00:00:59.850
to create the feeling of

00:00:59.850 --> 00:01:01.703
snowboarding on land.

00:01:06.245 --> 00:01:07.078
(calm music)

00:01:07.078 --> 00:01:08.560
So in the early '90s, my friend and I

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:10.434
decided to build a mountainboard.

00:01:10.434 --> 00:01:11.470
When we started making 'em

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.100
we really had no idea about

00:01:13.100 --> 00:01:16.350
any manufacturing techniques whatsoever.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:18.050
We'd go to auto part stores,

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.140
we'd go to junkyards,

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.443
and piece together

00:01:20.443 --> 00:01:22.690
these things to, you know,

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:24.880
make a functioning board.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:27.400
- We still had a frame
system at that point.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.560
- [Jason] Watching mountainboarding
grow from literally

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.173
our garage to a global phenomenon is

00:01:32.173 --> 00:01:34.460
incredibly satisfying.

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:36.130
There are mountainboarders

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:38.210
in probably over 30 countries right now.

00:01:38.210 --> 00:01:39.470
It was really important for us from

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.040
the very beginning to make sure that

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.420
it was not just a product,

00:01:43.420 --> 00:01:44.253
it was a sport.

00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:47.850
(upbeat electric guitar)

00:01:47.850 --> 00:01:50.520
It is, believe it or not, very easy to do.

00:01:50.520 --> 00:01:52.544
The coolest thing about
it, is that you can

00:01:52.544 --> 00:01:54.940
go out on an adventure

00:01:54.940 --> 00:01:56.170
anywhere you're at.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:58.830
So you don't have to
travel hours and hours

00:01:58.830 --> 00:02:00.643
or days to go some place cool.

00:02:02.910 --> 00:02:05.030
You can ride a mountainboard
anywhere you desire.

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:07.250
You can ride it on grass, dirt, pavement.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:09.810
You could ride it on dirt roads,

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:11.320
BMX tracks;

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:13.133
it's virtually limitless.

00:02:16.974 --> 00:02:18.550
(upbeat electric guitar)

00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:20.602
Mountainboarding has
brought a lot of friends

00:02:20.602 --> 00:02:22.220
into my life.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:24.840
And just kind of a feeling of community.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:27.900
It gives me a sense of
purpose to get outdoors

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.410
and maybe create some jumps.

00:02:29.410 --> 00:02:32.910
And being able to bring
mountainboarding to

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.970
people around the country,

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:35.803
around the world,

00:02:35.803 --> 00:02:36.800
is a fantastic feeling.

00:02:45.819 --> 00:02:48.236
(bell chime)

